{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"adfa775f-771e-4fe1-94a8-a296b2a87d66","step_index":16,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.147118,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"git log -p -n 5"},"output":"\u003ctruncated 226 lines\u003e\n+\r\n+I'd fixed a few harmless 404s and created a soft 404 on every new page.\r\n+\r\n+The fix was robots.txt only: allow the public read endpoints the pages need, and keep the POST-only and per-user ones blocked with longer, more specific rules. Google uses the most specific matching rule, so `Disallow: /v1/stories/*/reproduced` still beats `Allow: /v1/stories`.\r\n+\r\n+What happened next: Google re-crawled the site on October 2, the day of the fix. Two days later none of the ten pages I inspected was a soft 404 any more. The story that had been \"Soft 404\" and four others were now \"Crawled — currently not indexed\" (Google has read them and is deciding), /skills moved to \"Submitted and indexed\", and three were still waiting in the queue. Indexing itself takes longer on a young site, but the block is gone.\r\n+\r\n+## Reproduce this\r\n+\r\n+Prerequisites: a site whose pages are filled in by JavaScript from an API on the same domain (React, Vue, vanilla JS, anything), a verified Google Search Console property, and access to the site's `robots.txt`.\r\n+\r\n+Your agent will need from you: the site URL, the path prefix of your API (e.g. `/api/` or `/v1/`), and one URL that Search Console reports as \"Soft 404\" or \"Discovered – currently not indexed\".\r\n+\r\n+Steps:\r\n+1. Fetch `https://\u003csite\u003e/robots.txt`. List every `Disallow` rule that matches an address your page's JavaScript fetches while it renders (open the page with the browser's Network tab, or grep the app's source for `fetch(` / `axios`). Any match is a candidate cause: Googlebot renders the page without that data.\r\n+2. Check what the page shows when that fetch fails. If it's a \"not found\" or empty screen served with HTTP 200, that is exactly what Google classifies as a soft 404.\r\n+3. Rewrite robots.txt with Google's longest-match rule in mind: `Allow` the public read endpoints the pages need (`Allow: /v1/stories`), keep the general `Disallow: /v1/`, and re-block anything that must stay out with a longer rule (`Disallow: /v1/stories/*/reproduced`). Never unblock per-user or admin endpoints.\r\n+4. Test the rules the way Google evaluates them before deploying: for each path, the longest matching rule wins, and `Allow` wins a tie. A 20-line script is enough; don't use Python's `urllib.robotparser`, which applies first-match.\r\n+5. Deploy, then confirm the live file: `curl -s https://\u003csite\u003e/robots.txt`.\r\n+6. Optional but cheap: make sure the page's server-side HTML carries real `\u003ca href\u003e` links to your content, so Google can find pages without depending on the sitemap alone. Check with `curl -s https://\u003csite\u003e/ | grep -o 'href=\"/\u003ccontent-path\u003e/[^\"]*\"' | sort -u | wc -l`.\r\n+7. In Search Console: Settings → Crawling → robots.txt → Open report → ⋮ on your host → Request a recrawl. Then URL Inspection → Test live URL on the affected page, and Request indexing (about 10 URLs/day).\r\n+\r\n+Verify: URL Inspection → Test live URL on the page that was a soft 404 now reports that the page can be indexed, and the rendered screenshot shows the real content instead of your not-found screen. Within days to two weeks, the page moves to \"Indexed\" in the Pages report.\r\ndiff --git a/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv b/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..6729ff4\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\r\n+URL,Last crawled,Verdict,Reason\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/,2026-10-15,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/first-frost-dates,2026-08-29,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/mulch-depth-trial,2026-08-31,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure,2026-10-12,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/compost-thermometer-week-3,2026-10-13,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/soil-ph-kit-review,2026-10-14,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/rain-barrel-overflow,2026-10-10,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/bean-trellis-v2,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/greenhouse-vent-timer,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\r\ndiff --git a/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt b/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..efe0dab\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\r\n+URL: https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure\r\n+Live test, 2026-10-16\r\n+\r\n+Availability: URL is available to Google\r\n+Crawl: allowed (robots.txt)\r\n+Indexing: Page cannot be indexed: Soft 404\r\n+Page fetch: Successful (HTTP 200)\r\n+Rendered page title: \"Field notes\"\r\n+Rendered page text (excerpt): \"NOT FOUND  No note lives at this address.  Back to all notes\"\r\ndiff --git a/site/app.js b/site/app.js\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..18cc3f0\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/app.js\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\r\n+// Renders the home list or one note, depending on the path.\r\n+(async function () {\r\n+  const app = document.getElementById(\"app\");\r\n+  const m = location.pathname.match(/^\\/n\\/([a-z0-9-]+)$/);\r\n+  try {\r\n+    if (m) {\r\n+      const r = await fetch(`/v1/notes/${m[1]}`);\r\n+      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n+      const note = await r.json();\r\n+      document.title = `${note.title} · Field notes`;\r\n+      app.innerHTML = `\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch1\u003e${esc(note.title)}\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp class=\"meta\"\u003e${esc(note.date)}\u003c/p\u003e${note.html}\u003c/article\u003e`;\r\n+    } else {\r\n+      const r = await fetch(\"/v1/notes?limit=50\");\r\n+      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n+      const notes = await r.json();\r\n+      app.innerHTML = \"\u003cul\u003e\" + notes.map(n =\u003e `\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"/n/${n.slug}\"\u003e${esc(n.title)}\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e`).join(\"\") + \"\u003c/ul\u003e\";\r\n+    }\r\n+  } catch (e) {\r\n+    app.innerHTML = `\u003csection class=\"notfound\"\u003e\u003ch1\u003eNOT FOUND\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo note lives at this address.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/\"\u003eBack to all notes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/section\u003e`;\r\n+  }\r\n+  function esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[\u0026\u003c\u003e\"]/g, c =\u003e ({\"\u0026\":\"\u0026amp;\",\"\u003c\":\"\u0026lt;\",\"\u003e\":\"\u0026gt;\",'\"':\"\u0026quot;\"}[c])); }\r\n+})();\r\ndiff --git a/site/index.html b/site/index.html\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..83910e6\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/index.html\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\r\n+\u003c!doctype html\u003e\r\n+\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\r\n+\u003chead\u003e\r\n+\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\r\n+\u003ctitle\u003eField notes\u003c/title\u003e\r\n+\u003cmeta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,follow\"\u003e\r\n+\u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"\u003e\r\n+\u003c/head\u003e\r\n+\u003cbody\u003e\r\n+\u003cheader\u003e\u003ca href=\"/\"\u003eField notes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\r\n+\u003cmain id=\"app\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"loading\"\u003eLoading…\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/main\u003e\r\n+\u003cscript src=\"/app.js\"\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\r\n+\u003c/body\u003e\r\n+\u003c/html\u003e\r\ndiff --git a/site/robots.txt b/site/robots.txt\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..c8746c7\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/robots.txt\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\r\n+User-agent: *\r\n+Disallow: /v1/\r\n+Disallow: /admin/\r\n+\r\n+Sitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\r\ndiff --git a/site/sitemap.xml b/site/sitemap.xml\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..0f69c74\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/sitemap.xml\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\r\n+\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?\u003e\r\n+\u003curlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\"\u003e\r\n+  \u003curl\u003e\u003cloc\u003ehttps://fieldnotes.example/\u003c/loc\u003e\u003c/url\u003e\r\n+  \u003curl\u003e\u003cloc\u003ehttps://fieldnotes.example/n/soil-ph-kit-review\u003c/loc\u003e\u003clastmod\u003e2026-10-11\u003c/lastmod\u003e\u003c/url\u003e\r\n+  \u003curl\u003e\u003cloc\u003ehttps://fieldnotes.example/n/compost-thermometer-week-3\u003c/loc\u003e\u003clastmod\u003e2026-10-09\u003c/lastmod\u003e\u003c/url\u003e\r\n+  \u003curl\u003e\u003cloc\u003ehttps://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure\u003c/loc\u003e\u003clastmod\u003e2026-09-30\u003c/lastmod\u003e\u003c/url\u003e\r\n+  \u003curl\u003e\u003cloc\u003ehttps://fieldnotes.example/n/first-frost-dates\u003c/loc\u003e\u003clastmod\u003e2026-08-20\u003c/lastmod\u003e\u003c/url\u003e\r\n+  \u003c!-- 53 more --\u003e\r\n+\u003c/urlset\u003e\r\ndiff --git a/site/styles.css b/site/styles.css\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..5a88fc5\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/styles.css\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\r\n+body { font: 17px/1.5 Georgia, serif; max-width: 40rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }\r\n+.notfound { color: #933; }\r\n"}}}
