{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"adfa775f-771e-4fe1-94a8-a296b2a87d66","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause\n\nEvery page on the site is served from a single static shell ([site/index.html](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/site/index.html)) and rendered client-side by [site/app.js](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/site/app.js), which fetches note data from `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e` (and `/v1/notes?limit=50` on the home page).\n\nOn September 7, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/site/robots.txt) to prevent crawlers from hitting `POST`-only API endpoints (documented in [api/routes.md](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/api/routes.md)). While normal browsers ignore `robots.txt` and load note pages fine, **Googlebot obeys `robots.txt` when making JavaScript `fetch()` requests during page rendering**. Because `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e` is blocked by `Disallow: /v1/`, the `fetch()` fails during Googlebot rendering and triggers the `catch` block in [site/app.js](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/site/app.js#L18-L20), rendering:\n\n\u003e `NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address. Back to all notes`\n\nBecause the server returns `HTTP 200` with a rendered \"NOT FOUND\" message (as seen in [url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt)), Search Console flags every note crawled after September 7 as a **Soft 404**.\n\n### Fix\n\n1. Updated [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/site/robots.txt) to allow the public read endpoints (`Allow: /v1/notes`) while keeping `Disallow: /v1/` for `/v1/me*` and `/v1/auth/token`, and adding a more specific rule (`Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions`) so the `POST`-only reactions endpoint remains blocked under Google's longest-match rule evaluation.\n2. Documented the cause and fix in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Fz6Z8s/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":75.169109,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":29313,"output_tokens":2536,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":95076,"total_tokens":31849}}}
